<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<article>
  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <abstract>
        <p>A synthetic JATS fixture tests structured Review parsing without imported scientific content.</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>Structured XML provides explicit section boundaries for deterministic extraction.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Conceptual categories</title>
      <p>This thematic parent contains neutral validation language.</p>
      <sec>
        <title>Measurement boundaries</title>
        <p>The nested thematic child tests true parent-section identifiers.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec>
        <title>Reporting variation</title>
        <p>A second child allows sibling order to be checked.</p>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Open reporting questions</title>
      <p>A separate top-level theme must not disappear during canonical aggregation.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Conclusions</title>
      <p>The fixture remains a software test rather than a scientific source.</p>
    </sec>
  </body>
</article>
